# Swan Compiler 2 — SIL Optimization
#
# Optimize high-level SIL while source-language types and ownership semantics
# are still available.
#
# Planned pass order (passes become enabled only when verified):
# 1. SIL verification and canonicalization.
# 2. Constant propagation and constant folding.
# 3. Generic specialization and inlining where semantics permit.
# 4. Control-flow simplification and unreachable-block elimination.
# 5. SIL demand-driven dead-code elimination.
# 6. Ownership/lifetime optimization and retain/release elimination if used.
# 7. Devirtualization and dispatch simplification where proven safe.
# 8. Reverification after each transforming pass.
#
# Passes declare required analyses, preserved analyses, and invalidated
# analyses. No optimization may change observable behavior or ownership rules.
#
# Implementation status: contract; no complete SIL optimizer yet.
